## Implementation Details

The Analytics component is correctly implemented in the root layout:

```typescript
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        {children}
        <Analytics />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

This follows the official Next.js App Router pattern exactly as specified in the Vercel documentation.

## Additional Notes

- The project also has Cloudflare Web Analytics configured alongside Vercel Analytics
- Both analytics solutions can coexist without conflicts
- Speed Insights (`@vercel/speed-insights`) is not installed - this is a separate optional package for performance monitoring
- No custom event tracking or data redaction is configured (these are optional advanced features)

## Next Steps for Deployment

To activate Vercel Web Analytics on Vercel:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel (if not already deployed)
2. Navigate to your project dashboard on Vercel
3. Go to the Analytics tab
4. Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
5. Analytics data will start appearing after user visits

